# Seiche's speed dial through the main page's Speed select (physics catalog
# plan, ruled 2026-10-04, "Speed select" and "Target + Max, budget as frame
# share"): 1x by default; 50x applies when chosen, and on
# index.html?nodes=300&seed=7&links=none&gpu=off, too large for fifty CPU
# ticks in half a frame, the speed reached shows beneath the select; Max runs
# as fast as the budget allows; back at 1x the budget no longer binds.
assert title GRAPHSHELL H3 READY
assert snap ready == true
assert snap physics-speed == 1
click role:button @data-command=physics:toggle
settle 1
assert snap physics-paused == false
click role:combobox Arrangement
settle 1
click role:option Free (physics alone)
settle 1
click role:button Apply arrangement
settle 1
assert snap layout == free
click role:combobox Speed
settle 1
click role:option 50x
settle 1
settle 2
assert snap physics-speed == 50
assert retained {"role":"status","label":"Physics status","text":"Speed set to 50x"}
settle 40
assert snap physics-budget-share == 0.5
assert retained {"role":"status","label":"Speed status","text":"Reached"}
capture physics_speed_select_bound
click role:combobox Speed
settle 1
click role:option Max
settle 1
settle 2
assert snap physics-speed == max
assert retained {"role":"status","label":"Physics status","text":"Speed set to Max"}
settle 40
assert snap physics-budget-bound == true
assert retained {"role":"status","label":"Speed status","text":"the frame budget is full"}
click role:combobox Speed
settle 1
click role:option 1x
settle 1
settle 4
assert snap physics-speed == 1
assert snap physics-budget-bound == false
log physics speed select receipt complete
